<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Mount Fuji, pagoda and cherry blossoms (from 03-japanese-landscape.svg).
    The source 1024x560 artwork is cropped to the illustrated band
    (x = 0..730, y = 20..560) and given a soft sky base, so the strip always
    fills its box.

    The scene box is very wide and short at the widget's minimum size, and
    centreCrop trims roughly 12% off the top and the bottom. The composition
    is therefore pulled up into the band that survives that crop: the pagoda,
    the blossom clusters and the sea of clouds all sit higher than in the
    source, so the summit, the pagoda spire and the blossoms stay visible even
    in the shortest placement while the clouds still run off the bottom edge.
-->
